I wrote up a tourist skill slot strategy a while ago, well before I
developed my current system of how to write one.  The conclusions
aren't different, though.  Tourists have a ton of extra slots if they
don't avoid leveling up:

Tourist skills enhancement options

broadsword to Basic - 1  only Dragonbane or named Orcrist interesting

long sword to Basic - 1  Vorpy is crowning gift

short sword to Expert - 6  ridiculous

saber to Skilled - 3  GS not available just Werebane but great
secondary for #twoweapon

polearms to Basic - 1  straight shot only, mediocre for castles

hammer to Basic - 1  Mojo is neutral

dagger to Expert - 6  MB is neutral, Sting nameable, fill that quiver

knife to Skilled - 3  Ignore unless going for a crysknife game

axe to Basic - 1  only Cleaver is interesting

dart to Expert - 6  ridiculous

unihorn to Skilled - 3  may be worth it

pickaxe to Basic - 1

twoweapon to Skilled - 3  extremely important


1) Enhance dagger toward Expert, start throwing them as replacements
for
the initial stock of darts.  6 slots leaving 23

2) Twoweapon with daggers toward Skilled.  3 slots leaving 20

3) Pickaxe to Basic.  1 slot leaving 19

4) If minetown gives silver saber, to Skilled.  3 slots leaving 16

5) Hammer and long sword as they appear at sacfest.  2 slots leaving 14

6) Polearm to basic after first troll leaves a spetum.  1 slot leaving
13

7) Spell schools in any order.  Divination Basic 1.  Enchantment Basic
1.
Escape Skilled 2.  4 slots leaving 9.

8) Advance each interesting artifact for style points.

Divination spells - detect monsters, light, detect food, clarvoyance,
detect unseen, identify, detect treasure, magic mapping.  Practice
with detect monsters.  Detect unseen for the planes.  Identify for
sacfests.  Magic mapping for Gehennom.

Enchanment spells - sleep, confuse monster, slow monster, cause fear,
charm monster.  Sleep works as a combat spell so use it for practice.

Escape spells - jumping, haste self, invisibility, leviation, teleport
away.  Practice with jumping.



